{"resourceIdentifier":"3071","resourceName":"KARACABEY BIOGAS PLANT","description":"The project is a biogas-to-energy project that generates renewable energy by capturing biogas from animal manure -via anaerobic digestion- and utilizing it to produce thermal and electric energy through biogas systems. The project is being implemented by KARACABEY BIYOGAZ ENERJI URETIM ANONİM ŞİRKETİ, as the Project Owner, in Karacabey district, BURSA province, in Turkey.\r\n\r\nCattle and chicken manure which are generated at farms and left to decay in anaerobic conditions are collected daily through special sewage trucks equipped with close tanks to prevent any odour and/or manure leakages and to be fed into the anaerobic digesters at the proposed biogas power plant. \r\n\r\nThe project has received Electricity Generation License (EGL) issued by the Energy Market Regulatory Authority (EMRA) in Turkey on June 3rd, 2021, for the maximum operational licenced capacity of 3.002 MWe/h. The proposed project activity currently has two biogas engines installed at the biogas power plant, with the capacity of 1,501 KWe/h each. Heat generated at the plant is used at the facility to warm the digesters, the electricity generated is directly fed to the national grid.  \r\n\r\nThe project has become operational by starting to generate electricity and feeding it directly to the Turkish national grid on June 27th, 2021. \r\n\r\nThis project adopts the renewable crediting period of 7 years, twice renewable for a total of 21 years. The estimated average net annual emission reductions are 490,374 tCO2eq/y. Accordingly, the project is expected to generate 3,432,618 tCO2eq/y emissions reduction during the first crediting period.","location":{"latitude":40.222880,"longitude":28.366560},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2022-09-06","endExclusive":"2022-10-07","endInclusive":"2022-10-06"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"3071"}]}